.TH GPS 1 2000-1月 "build_gps" "build_gps"
.SH NAME
build_gps \- Build a GPS (GNN + Transformer) gene regulatory network model.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIbuild_gps(\fBx\fR as <generic> GeneExpressionData, 
\fBprior\fR as <generic> PriorNetwork, 
\fBconfig\fR as <generic> GPSConfig = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Build a GPS (GNN + Transformer) gene regulatory network model.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBx\fB \fR\- 
 the time series gene expression matrix object: rows are genes and columns are samples,
 and every sample must carry a time point label (for example the matrix loaded by
 \fBgeneExpression::load.expr\fR). At least three distinct time points are required.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBprior\fB \fR\- 
 the prior regulatory network object (for example created by
 \fBbnlearn::as.prior_net\fR). Gene pairs that are not described by this network are kept as
 isolated nodes and still participate in the global attention branch.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBconfig\fB \fR\- 
 the hyper-parameter configuration created by \fBgps::gps_config\fR; when \fBNothing\fR the
 default [GPSConfig](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.GPS.Config.GPSConfig) values are used. Note that the window length may be
 clipped when the input has too few time points.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
an untrained [GPSModel](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.GPS.GPSModel) object
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
The constructor performs the following preparation steps once and keeps the results,
 so they are reused by every training epoch and by the virtual perturbation analysis:
 


 
1. preprocessing: CPM normalization, \fBlog2(x + 1)\fR transformation, per gene z-score and
 the optional high variance gene filter;
2. graph construction: the prior \fBTF -> target\fR edges are mapped onto the modelled genes,
 optionally extended with co-expression edges;
3. static graph encoding: shortest path distance buckets, Laplacian positional encoding and
 the in/out degree buckets;
4. the strictly time ordered train / validation / test split of the sliding windows.


 


 The returned object is untrained; call \fBgps::train\fR before any prediction or
 perturbation analysis. It can also be persisted with the \fBwriteBin\fR handler and
 restored with \fBreadBin.modular_bayesian\fR.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
GPS
